# Patterns without a `**/` prefix are anchored at the context root, so `data`
# alone matches `/data` and nothing else. The dev database actually lives at
# `apps/backend/data/`, which is exactly the kind of thing that must never be
# baked into a published image — hence `**/` on anything that could appear
# under a workspace directory.

# Dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# IDE
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Build artifacts
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.log

# Tests (not needed in the runtime image)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.integration.test.ts

# Local databases. A developer's copy holds real member records — contact
# details and allergies — so this is the one group where a missed pattern
# publishes personal data to Docker Hub.
**/data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm

# Documentation. Two exceptions, both served by the app rather than read here: `CHANGELOG.md`
# at `/changelog`, and `PRIVACY.md` at `/privacy`. `CHANGELOG.md` is the exception:
# which is where the "a new version is out" notification leads, so it is part of the
# image rather than something a reader of the repository sees (#325).
**/*.md
!CHANGELOG.md
# And the privacy policy, which `/privacy` serves and Facebook's app review reads (#402).
!PRIVACY.md
docs

# Environment files (passed in as env vars instead)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# OS files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
